(* README *)

1 - Summary
    -------

    L002 formalizes SYMBOLIC REGULATION as a clean M001-native
    operational non-escape and recursive-approximation layer.

    Final deliverable invariant:

      embedded_authority_stability_limit

    Formally, regulator-admissible authority internalizes locally, embedded
    local derivability transports to the enclosing regulator, and stable
    continuation supplies a finite bound on recursive pressure. This is the
    package's unifying operational theorem.

    The package also exposes a concrete one-state model pattern. That pattern
    instantiates the abstract recursive-pressure interfaces with a specific
    authority formula, counter-approximation relation, depth-indexed penalty,
    and bounded-pressure stability predicate.

    The package works with regulator-conditioned local authority over one
    context:

      Slambda : RegulatorTheory     -- object-level symbolic regulator Sλ
      M : RegulatorTheory     -- internal model
      Gamma : Context

    Rocq itself remains the ambient proof theory `T`; `Slambda`/`Sλ` names the
    regulator represented inside the object-level formalization.

    The primitive explanatory surface is:

      AsIF : Type

    An `asif A` hypothesis means that the regulator authorizes local
    operational continuation under `A`. It is not semantic truth, belief,
    self-knowledge, or M/Sλ equivalence.

    The retained mirror-wrapper theorem also keeps two compatibility
    parameters:

      code_Slambda_derives : CodingOfSLambdaDerivability
      chi_eq         : DiagonalFormula

    `code_Slambda_derives` is a Formula-valued coding operator for the claim that
    `Sλ` derives a formula. `chi_eq` is the retained witness
    formula used by the mirror-wrapper theorem. It is no longer the conceptual
    center of L002.

    The proof-minimal kernel is:

      mirror_unrefutability_core :
        ChiEqMInternal M Gamma chi_eq ->
        MirrorConsistent M Gamma ->
        ~ regulator_theory_checked_derivable M Gamma
            (formula_negation chi_eq)

    The public full-interface wrapper is:

      mirror_unrefutability :
        regulator_theory_included M Slambda ->
        InternalInclusionViaCoding M Gamma code_Slambda_derives ->
        CodingInternalAccuracy M Gamma code_Slambda_derives ->
        DiagonalEliminator Slambda M Gamma chi_eq ->
        ChiEqMInternal M Gamma chi_eq ->
        MirrorConsistent M Gamma ->
        ~ regulator_theory_checked_derivable M Gamma
            (formula_negation chi_eq)

    The proof-minimal kernel and full-interface wrapper are constructive and
    M001-native. The grouped operational layer imports L001 to build an
    existential `chi_eq` satisfying the M-side Curry property. The premise
    layer also fixes the canonical operational vocabulary:

      AsIF       -- regulator-admissible local authority
      AsIFFor    -- model-indexed AsIF(M,A)
      Escape     -- local checked realization of an escape claim
      RecursiveApproximationStructure
        approximates : Model -> Formula -> Prop
        RecursiveDepth : Model -> Formula -> nat -> Prop
        Penalty      : Model -> nat
        PenaltyAtDepth : nat -> Model -> nat
        Stable       : Model -> Prop
        Fragmented   : Model -> Prop

    No layer assumes classical excluded middle, introduces an arithmetic
    provability predicate, or uses an Axiom or Parameter command.


